  "interpretation": [
    "Encoding/handoff is about 2x faster and removes the complete Go-owned encoded payload and its native copy.",
    "Durable batch timings remain close and are fsync-sensitive; do not interpret the isolated codec speedup as a 2x total ingress improvement.",
    "Native peak bytes in the durable comparison are unchanged. Inputs and published outputs retain independent immutable native spans.",
    "Sealing sample ranges overlap and have outliers; no sealing speedup is established.",
    "Go still owns field descriptors, scalar scratch, maps and other metadata. This does not claim zero Go allocation throughout ingress."
  ],
